    "PMC",
    "NCBI PubMed"
  ],
  "description": "The authoritative biomedical and life sciences literature index maintained by the US National Library of Medicine (NLM/NCBI). Covers 35M+ citations from MEDLINE, PubMed Central (PMC), and in-process records. Structured with MeSH (Medical Subject Headings) controlled vocabulary enabling precise clinical and biomedical retrieval. Free E-utilities API (eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov) with no authentication required for basic access; API key available for higher rate limits. PMC provides open-access full text for 4M+ articles. The primary source for verifying peer-reviewed biomedical literature — gold standard for discovering papers associated with clinical software, AI models, and healthcare tools. Used by Elicit, Europe PMC, and virtually every biomedical literature discovery platform as the foundational data source.",
